`memory_init.wast` (task #95) needed real new interpreter state --
`memory.init`/`data.drop` (0xFC 0x08/0x09) were entirely unimplemented
before this pass (no opcode decoding, no interpreter handler, no
wast-parser text-form support, no validator type-check rule), and
neither can work without real PASSIVE data segments (`(data $d
"bytes")`, no offset expression): `wasm-module-parser`'s binary decoder
only ever handled segment-mode flag `0x00` (active, implicit memory 0)
before this, not the real 3-mode encoding the bulk-memory proposal
defines. 100% pass, every directive kind, on the first baseline regen
after implementation. Only uses single-memory numeric segment indices
(no `spectest` import, no table/elem instructions), so it's vendorable
standalone -- unlike its sibling `bulk.wast` (task #97 still pending)
and `memory-multi.wast` (task #92, explicit multi-memory indices, was
blocked on real multi-memory memarg support).

